  body: |
    # Reassessment and conversion of legacy awards to ESA

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source calls the process of deciding whether existing IB, SDA or disability-related IS awards qualify for conversion to ESA reassessment, with an existing award potentially including more than one benefit.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 45300–45302 describe a process beginning in 2010 and national staging in 2011. The credits-only exclusion and other IS categories at 45306/45315 qualify scope. This historical conversion is not equated with a new claim or UC managed migration.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 45300, PDF page 16](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6717a7f6194d62fb6854056b/dmg-chapter-45-ib-sda-and-is-claims-and-reassessment.pdf#page=16)
    - [DMG 45301, PDF page 16](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6717a7f6194d62fb6854056b/dmg-chapter-45-ib-sda-and-is-claims-and-reassessment.pdf#page=16)
    - [DMG 45302, PDF page 16](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6717a7f6194d62fb6854056b/dmg-chapter-45-ib-sda-and-is-claims-and-reassessment.pdf#page=16)
    - [DMG 45306, PDF page 17](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6717a7f6194d62fb6854056b/dmg-chapter-45-ib-sda-and-is-claims-and-reassessment.pdf#page=17)
